{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:28.092Z","tool_name":"update_topic","tool_id":"update_topic__call_358886","parameters":{"strategic_intent":"Independently verify the structural lemma, case analysis, and witnesses, and coordinate with sol on answer.md.","title":"Verifying Structural Lemma and External Stability Cases","summary":"Both sol and I independently discovered the fundamental lemma that two distinct allocations are incomparable under dominance iff they share a coordinate. Consequently, every internally stable set is either collinear (a subset of a single coordinate line x_i = c) or a non-collinear triangle of 3 points defined by x_1 = a, x_2 = b, x_3 = c. I am now verifying all cases and witnesses for external stability and coordinating with sol on the final proof in /work/answer.md."}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:30.083Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_358897","parameters":{"command":"python3 -c '\nimport datetime\nnow = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC\")\nwith open(\"/work/board.md\", \"a\") as f:\n    f.write(f\"[argon] {now}: Independently derived the same structural lemma (x, y incomparable iff x_i = y_i for some i, so internally stable sets are either subsets of a line x_i = c or a 3-point triangle). Now independently verifying all cases and witnesses for external stability.\\n\")\n'","description":"Append status update to /work/board.md via Python"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:36.595Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_358933","parameters":{"command":"python3 -c '\ndef dominates(x, y):\n    return (x[0] > y[0] and x[1] > y[1]) or (x[0] > y[0] and x[2] > y[2]) or (x[1] > y[1] and x[2] > y[2])\n\n# Verify exhaustively for K=2..15 that:\n# 1) Every internally stable set is either collinear or a triangle of 3 points.\n# 2) Check all collinear subsets and all triangles for K=2..30.\nfor K in range(2, 21):\n    pts = [(a, b, K - a - b) for a in range(K + 1) for b in range(K + 1 - a)]\n    # Check all triangles: defined by a, b, c >= 0 with a+b <= K, a+c <= K, b+c <= K, a+b+c != K\n    stable_found = []\n    for a in range(K + 1):\n        for b in range(K + 1):\n            for c in range(K + 1):\n                if a + b <= K and a + c <= K and b + c <= K and a + b + c != K:\n                    V = [(K - b - c, b, c), (a, K - a - c, c), (a, b, K - a - b)]\n                    internal = any(dominates(x, y) for x in V for y in V)\n                    assert not internal\n                    external = [y for y in pts if y not in V and not any(dominates(x, y) for x in V)]\n                    if not external:\n                        stable_found.append(set(V))\n    # Also check maximal collinear sets (if a subset of a line is externally stable, adding the rest of the line keeps it externally stable, except wait: if y is on the line and not in V, can another point on the line dominate y? NO! Points on the same line cannot dominate each other! So if V is a subset of a line and externally stable, V MUST be the entire line!)\n    for i in range(3):\n        for c in range(K + 1):\n            V = [p for p in pts if p[i] == c]\n            external = [y for y in pts if y not in V and not any(dominates(x, y) for x in V)]\n            if not external:\n                stable_found.append(set(V))\n    print(f\"K={K}: stable_found = {stable_found}\")\n'","description":"Verify all collinear and triangle sets for K=2..20"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:38.078Z","tool_id":"update_topic__call_358886","status":"success","output":"## 📂 Topic: **Verifying Structural Lemma and External Stability Cases**\n\n**Summary:**\nBoth sol and I independently discovered the fundamental lemma that two distinct allocations are incomparable under dominance iff they share a coordinate. Consequently, every internally stable set is either collinear (a subset of a single coordinate line x_i = c) or a non-collinear triangle of 3 points defined by x_1 = a, x_2 = b, x_3 = c. I am now verifying all cases and witnesses for external stability and coordinating with sol on the final proof in /work/answer.md.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Independently verify the structural lemma, case analysis, and witnesses, and coordinate with sol on answer.md."}
